#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Street Legends backend: Brown Sugar enemy-drop item (backend / Publish).

USER SPEC (exact, 2026-11-05 09:11 EST, with his photo): item name
"Brown Sugar"; sells for $500 per oz; when collected it goes into the
player's item screen (inventory). Art is the uploaded pink-bag brown
sugar image, embedded below as a data-URI icon_url (the GitHub push
tool cannot carry binary files, so no raw GitHub URL is used; the
uploaded file is JPEG data despite the .png name, so the URI uses
image/jpeg; if the client cannot render the data URI, the row falls
back to the clover icon and the item still functions).

READINGS (NOT the user's decisions - correctable):
- "1 - 20 fights" is read as a 1-in-20 chance EACH fight, following the
  user's own correction on Pills (where "1 - 6" meant 1-in-6 per fight,
  not a 1-to-6-fight gap). Flat 5% roll on every standard battle
  victory, 1 oz when it lands, any enemy type. NOT an interval counter,
  NO random-gap counter. PvP and guild-raid victories have no loot path in the
  snapshot and are not hooked.
- Use: consumes 1 oz; for 60 seconds luck is 50% higher. NEW RULE (user,
  09:11 EST, extended 09:15 EST "For other 4 also"): the player can only
  use the same item once until the effect wears off - this applies to ALL
  FIVE items (Brown Sugar + Grass + Pills + Rock Candy + Flake). A second
  use while that item's buff is active is REJECTED server-side WITHOUT
  consuming the oz (HTTP 400, "<Item> is already active - wait for the
  effect to wear off."). It does NOT refresh the timer. When the buff
  expires, the player may use it again. Each item is checked against its
  OWN buff only (Grass active blocks Grass, not Pills). This patch adds
  the rule to Brown Sugar's own endpoint AND retrofits the four existing
  use endpoints (part 7) - their buffs, drop rates, and sell behavior are
  NOT changed, only the re-use rule (refresh-on-reuse becomes
  blocked-on-reuse).
- Sell: $500 per oz, 1 oz per tap, from the item screen, no prompt.

LUCK (investigated in the snapshot before implementing - server.py):
- luck IS a real player stat: base_stats include "luck", and
  get_effective_stats() returns a copy of player stats with a broken
  accessory forcing luck = 0. Luck is READ at exactly three sites in
  battle_action (standard monster battles only):
    1. Miss chance: miss_chance = max(0.05, 0.10 - luck*0.005);
       luck <= 0 means a 25% miss chance.
    2. Crit chance: crit_chance = 0.05 + luck*0.01 (0 if luck <= 0);
       a crit deals 2x damage.
    3. Generic loot drop: drop_chance = 0.3 + luck*0.02 (30% base +
       2% per luck), rolled on monster-battle victory.
  The +50% luck buff is therefore a live multiplier on the luck value
  at those three sites (this patch's LUCK HOOK), computed expiry-checked
  from the active buff - the same pattern as Flake's defense hook.
  Skill crit (flat 10%) and skill miss (flat 5%) do NOT read luck and
  are not changed. The PvP matchup path and the guild-raid path read
  luck from raw stats (or use flat crit) and are NOT hooked - same scope
  as the drop (standard monster battles only). The four consumable
  items' own drop rolls are flat rates (1/4, 1/6, 1/10, 1/15) that never
  read luck, so Brown Sugar does NOT change them; only the three
  luck-reading sites above get the boost. No new stat is invented:
  player_stats itself is never mutated (it also feeds level-up stat
  growth, which must stay unboosted). NOTE: if the accessory is broken,
  effective luck is 0 and 0 x 1.5 is still 0, so Brown Sugar gives no
  benefit until the accessory is repaired (same edge as Flake's broken
  armor).

Design notes (mirroring the Grass/Pills/Rock Candy/Flake patches; live
/app may differ, hence guards; this patch is STANDALONE - it never
assumes prior item code ran, but it IS order-tolerant of them: the pool
exclusion extends a pool line already modified by Grass, Pills, Rock
Candy, and/or Flake):
- Inventory is player["inventory"], a list of item_id strings or dicts;
  Brown Sugar is stored as ONE stacked dict {"item_id": "brown_sugar",
  "qty": N, "unit": "oz", ...} rather than one entry per oz.
- Brown Sugar is added to ALL_ITEMS so the inventory-details endpoint
  returns it (items absent from ALL_ITEMS are invisible on the item
  screen). It is EXCLUDED from the generic random drop pool so it
  cannot double-drop.
- Buffs live in player["active_buffs"] as {type: "luck", percent,
  ...}. Brown Sugar reuses that system with an expires_at timestamp plus
  a large battles_remaining (10000) so the time expiry - not the
  per-battle decrement - is what ends it. The once-only rule is enforced
  in the use endpoint by checking for an unexpired brown_sugar buff
  BEFORE consuming anything.
- The generic sell endpoint pays value//2 and pops one whole entry, so
  it must NOT be used for Brown Sugar: dedicated use/sell endpoints below pay
  exactly $500/oz and decrement qty. The frontend hides the generic
  Sell/Equip buttons for Brown Sugar rows.
- RUN ORDER: Grass -> Pills -> Rock Candy -> Flake -> Brown Sugar.
  This patch tolerates pool lines already modified by any subset of the
  prior four, but the prior patches use exact-match or narrower pool
  anchors and do NOT tolerate a brown-sugar-modified line: if Brown
  Sugar runs first, their pool parts print a WARNING and that item could
  double-drop from the generic pool.
"""
import re, sys
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else Path("/app")
SRV = ROOT / "backend/server.py"

BROWN_SUGAR_URL = "data:image/jpeg;base64,"

CATALOG = '''
# BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_CATALOG: Brown Sugar enemy-drop item (see patch header for spec/readings).
ALL_ITEMS["brown_sugar"] = {
    "id": "brown_sugar", "name": "Brown Sugar", "category": "consumable",
    "description": "Bag of brown sugar. Use: +50% luck for 60 seconds. Sells for $500 per oz.",
    "icon": "clover", "icon_url": ''' + '"' + BROWN_SUGAR_URL + '"' + ''',
    "rarity": "common", "equipment_type": "consumable",
    "stats_bonus": {}, "level_requirement": 1, "value": 500,
}
'''

ROUTES = '''
# BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_USE / BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_SELL: dedicated Brown Sugar endpoints ($500/oz, 1 oz per sell tap).
@api_router.post("/players/{player_id}/brown_sugar/use")
async def use_brown_sugar(player_id: str):
    """Use 1 oz of Brown Sugar: +50% luck for 60 seconds. Once only: rejected while active."""
    player = await db.players.find_one({"id": player_id})
    if not player:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Player not found")
    # BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_ONCE_ONLY: if the buff is still active, reject WITHOUT consuming.
    _bs_now = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()
    for _bs_b in player.get("active_buffs", []):
        if _bs_b.get("type") == "luck" and _bs_b.get("item_id") == "brown_sugar":
            _bs_exp = _bs_b.get("expires_at")
            if (not _bs_exp) or (str(_bs_exp) >= _bs_now):
                raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="Brown Sugar is already active - wait for the effect to wear off.")
    inv = player.get("inventory", [])
    f_idx = None
    f_qty = 0
    for _i, _it in enumerate(inv):
        if isinstance(_it, dict) and _it.get("item_id") == "brown_sugar":
            f_idx, f_qty = _i, _it.get("qty", 1)
            break
        if isinstance(_it, str) and _it == "brown_sugar":
            f_idx, f_qty = _i, 1
            break
    if f_idx is None or f_qty < 1:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="No Brown Sugar in inventory")
    if f_qty <= 1:
        inv.pop(f_idx)
    elif isinstance(inv[f_idx], dict):
        inv[f_idx]["qty"] = f_qty - 1
    else:
        inv.pop(f_idx)
    stats = player.get("stats", {})
    base_luck = stats.get("luck", 0)
    gain = int(base_luck * 0.5)
    boosted_luck = int(base_luck * 1.5)
    expiry = (datetime.utcnow() + timedelta(minutes=1)).isoformat()
    buffs = [b for b in player.get("active_buffs", []) if b.get("item_id") != "brown_sugar"]
    buffs.append({
        "id": "brown_sugar_" + str(uuid.uuid4())[:8], "item_id": "brown_sugar", "name": "Brown Sugar",
        "type": "luck", "amount": gain, "percent": 0.5,
        "battles_remaining": 10000, "expires_at": expiry, "icon": "clover",
    })
    await db.players.update_one(
        {"id": player_id},
        {"$set": {"inventory": inv, "active_buffs": buffs}},
    )
    return {"message": "Brown Sugar used! +50% luck for 60 seconds.", "base_luck": base_luck,
            "boosted_luck": boosted_luck, "expires_at": expiry, "oz_left": f_qty - 1}


@api_router.post("/players/{player_id}/brown_sugar/sell")
async def sell_brown_sugar(player_id: str, qty: int = 1):
    """Sell Brown Sugar at $500 per oz."""
    if qty < 1:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="Quantity must be at least 1")
    player = await db.players.find_one({"id": player_id})
    if not player:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Player not found")
    inv = player.get("inventory", [])
    f_idx = None
    f_qty = 0
    for _i, _it in enumerate(inv):
        if isinstance(_it, dict) and _it.get("item_id") == "brown_sugar":
            f_idx, f_qty = _i, _it.get("qty", 1)
            break
        if isinstance(_it, str) and _it == "brown_sugar":
            f_idx, f_qty = _i, 1
            break
    if f_idx is None or f_qty < qty:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="Not enough Brown Sugar in inventory")
    if f_qty <= qty:
        inv.pop(f_idx)
        left = 0
    elif isinstance(inv[f_idx], dict):
        inv[f_idx]["qty"] = f_qty - qty
        left = f_qty - qty
    else:
        inv.pop(f_idx)
        left = 0
    gained = 500 * qty
    await db.players.update_one(
        {"id": player_id},
        {"$set": {"inventory": inv}, "$inc": {"cash": gained}},
    )
    return {"message": f"Sold {qty} oz of Brown Sugar for ${gained}", "cash_gained": gained, "oz_left": left}

'''


def main():
    if not SRV.exists():
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_ERROR: backend/server.py not found (run from /app)")
        return 1
    src = SRV.read_text(errors="ignore")
    orig = src
    landed = []

    # 1. Catalog entry.
    if "BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_CATALOG" in src:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_CATALOG_ALREADY_APPLIED"); landed.append("catalog")
    else:
        anchor = "# Apply icon URLs to all equipment items"
        fallback = "ALL_ITEMS.update(LEVEL_ACCESSORIES)"
        if anchor in src:
            src = src.replace(anchor, CATALOG.strip() + "\n\n" + anchor, 1)
            print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_CATALOG_OK"); landed.append("catalog")
        elif fallback in src:
            src = src.replace(fallback, fallback + "\n" + CATALOG.strip(), 1)
            print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_CATALOG_OK"); landed.append("catalog")
        else:
            print("WARNING: catalog anchor not found - Brown Sugar NOT added to ALL_ITEMS (item will be invisible on the item screen)")

    # 2. Exclude Brown Sugar from the generic random drop pool (no double-drop).
    #    Tolerates a pool line already modified by Grass, Pills, Rock Candy, and/or Flake.
    if 'item["id"] != "brown_sugar"' in src:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_POOL_EXCLUDE_ALREADY_APPLIED"); landed.append("pool")
    else:
        pool_re = re.compile(r'if ((?:item\["id"\] != "[a-z_]+" and )*item\["level_requirement"\] <= enemy\["level"\] \+ 2)')
        m = pool_re.search(src)
        if m:
            src = src[:m.start(1)] + 'item["id"] != "brown_sugar" and ' + src[m.start(1):]
            print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_POOL_EXCLUDE_OK"); landed.append("pool")
        else:
            print("WARNING: generic drop-pool anchor not found - Brown Sugar may ALSO drop from the generic pool, so it could double-drop")

    # 3. Dedicated 1-in-20-per-fight drop on monster-battle victory.
    if "BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_DROP" in src:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_DROP_ALREADY_APPLIED"); landed.append("drop")
    else:
        loot_at = src.find('combat_log.append(f"Loot drop: {dropped_item[\'name\']}!")')
        if loot_at == -1:
            print("WARNING: victory loot anchor not found - Brown Sugar drop NOT added (no defeat hook)")
        else:
            upd_at = src.find("# Update player stats", loot_at)
            if upd_at == -1:
                print("WARNING: victory update anchor not found - Brown Sugar drop NOT added (no defeat hook)")
            else:
                drop = ('            # BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_DROP: READING - 1-in-20 chance EACH fight (flat 5% roll), 1 oz, any monster enemy.\n'
                        '            if random.random() < (1/20):\n'
                        '                _bs_inv = player.get("inventory", [])\n'
                        '                _bs_idx = next((i for i, _it in enumerate(_bs_inv) if isinstance(_it, dict) and _it.get("item_id") == "brown_sugar"), None)\n'
                        '                if _bs_idx is None:\n'
                        '                    _bs_inv.append({"item_id": "brown_sugar", "qty": 1, "unit": "oz", "durability": 100, "max_durability": 100})\n'
                        '                else:\n'
                        '                    _bs_inv[_bs_idx]["qty"] = _bs_inv[_bs_idx].get("qty", 1) + 1\n'
                        '                await db.players.update_one({"id": player["id"]}, {"$set": {"inventory": _bs_inv}})\n'
                        '                rewards["items"] = (rewards.get("items") or []) + ["brown_sugar"]\n'
                        '                combat_log.append("Loot drop: Brown Sugar (1 oz)!")\n'
                        )
                src = src[:upd_at] + drop + src[upd_at:]
                print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_DROP_OK"); landed.append("drop")

    # 4. Inventory-details qty/unit passthrough (shared with Grass/Pills/Rock Candy/Flake;
    #    whichever patch runs first adds it, the rest skip).
    if ("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_QTY" in src or "FLAKE_ITEM_QTY" in src or "ROCK_CANDY_ITEM_QTY" in src
            or "PILLS_ITEM_QTY" in src or "GRASS_ITEM_QTY" in src):
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_QTY_ALREADY_APPLIED"); landed.append("qty")
    else:
        anchor = 'item_with_durability["inventory_index"] = idx'
        if anchor in src:
            add = ('\n            # BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_QTY / FLAKE_ITEM_QTY / ROCK_CANDY_ITEM_QTY / PILLS_ITEM_QTY / GRASS_ITEM_QTY: pass stacked quantities through to the item screen.\n'
                   '            if inv_item.get("qty") is not None:\n'
                   '                item_with_durability["qty"] = inv_item["qty"]\n'
                   '            if inv_item.get("unit"):\n'
                   '                item_with_durability["unit"] = inv_item["unit"]')
            src = src.replace(anchor, anchor + add, 1)
            print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_QTY_OK"); landed.append("qty")
        else:
            print("WARNING: inventory-details anchor not found - oz count will NOT reach the item screen (Brown Sugar will show without a quantity)")

    # 5. Luck hook: live luck multiplier at the three luck-reading sites in battle_action.
    #    (No start_battle sum is touched: this hook checks expiry itself.)
    if "BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK" in src:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK_ALREADY_APPLIED"); landed.append("luck")
    else:
        stats_anchor = "player_stats = await get_effective_stats(player)"
        if stats_anchor not in src:
            print("WARNING: battle stats anchor not found - LUCK HOOK NOT ADDED, need a live snippet of battle_action where player_stats is computed")
        else:
            flag = ('\n    # BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK: a live Brown Sugar buff multiplies luck by (1 + percent) for 60s.\n'
                    '    # Expiry-checked here; player_stats itself is NOT mutated\n'
                    '    # (it also feeds level-up stat growth, which must stay unboosted).\n'
                    '    _bs_now_iso = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n'
                    '    _bs_luck_mult = 1.0\n'
                    '    for _bs_b in player.get("active_buffs", []):\n'
                    '        if _bs_b.get("type") == "luck" and _bs_b.get("item_id") == "brown_sugar":\n'
                    '            _bs_exp = _bs_b.get("expires_at")\n'
                    '            if (not _bs_exp) or (str(_bs_exp) >= _bs_now_iso):\n'
                    '                _bs_luck_mult = max(_bs_luck_mult, 1 + float(_bs_b.get("percent", 0.5)))')
            src = src.replace(stats_anchor, stats_anchor + flag, 1)
            ok = True
            # 5a. Miss + crit sites both read luck_val (one assignment, in the attack loop).
            luck_old = '            luck_val = player_stats.get("luck", 0)'
            if luck_old in src:
                src = src.replace(luck_old,
                    '            luck_val = int(player_stats.get("luck", 0) * _bs_luck_mult)  # BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK', 1)
            else:
                print("WARNING: battle miss/crit luck anchor not found - miss and crit chances will NOT get the Brown Sugar boost")
                ok = False
            # 5b. Generic loot-drop site reads luck directly.
            drop_old = 'drop_chance = 0.3 + (player_stats.get("luck", 0) * 0.02)'
            if drop_old in src:
                src = src.replace(drop_old,
                    'drop_chance = 0.3 + (int(player_stats.get("luck", 0) * _bs_luck_mult) * 0.02)  # BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK', 1)
            else:
                print("WARNING: victory loot-drop luck anchor not found - the generic drop chance will NOT get the Brown Sugar boost")
                ok = False
            if ok:
                print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK_OK"); landed.append("luck")
            else:
                print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_LUCK_PARTIAL: multiplier flag added but a luck site was missed")

    # 6. Use + sell endpoints.
    if "BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_USE" in src and "BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_SELL" in src:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_ENDPOINTS_ALREADY_APPLIED"); landed.append("endpoints")
    else:
        inc = "app.include_router(api_router)"
        if inc in src and "datetime" in src and "timedelta" in src and "uuid" in src:
            src = src.replace(inc, ROUTES.strip() + "\n\n\n" + inc, 1)
            print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_ENDPOINTS_OK"); landed.append("endpoints")
        else:
            print("WARNING: router anchor or datetime/timedelta/uuid imports not found - Brown Sugar use/sell endpoints NOT added")

    # 7. Once-only retrofit: the same active-buff rejection for the four existing items.
    #    Each item is checked against its OWN buff only. Buffs, drop rates, and sells are untouched.
    #    Anchors on the use-endpoint route decorator + its player 404 check (not the function
    #    name, which Emergent may have renamed); inserts the guard right after the 404 line.
    _once_items = [
        ("grass", "max_health", "Grass"),
        ("pills", "max_energy", "Pills"),
        ("rock_candy", "attack", "Rock Candy"),
        ("flake", "defense", "Flake"),
    ]
    _once_done = []
    for _oi_id, _oi_type, _oi_name in _once_items:
        _oi_marker = "BROWN_SUGAR_ONCE_ONLY_" + _oi_id.upper()
        if _oi_marker in src:
            print("BROWN_SUGAR_ONCE_ONLY_%s_ALREADY_APPLIED" % _oi_id.upper()); _once_done.append(_oi_id); continue
        _oi_route = '@api_router.post("/players/{player_id}/%s/use")' % _oi_id
        _oi_at = src.find(_oi_route)
        if _oi_at == -1:
            print("WARNING: %s use endpoint not found - once-only rule NOT added for %s" % (_oi_name, _oi_name)); continue
        _oi_raise = src.find('raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Player not found")', _oi_at)
        if _oi_raise == -1:
            print("WARNING: %s use endpoint player-check not found - once-only rule NOT added for %s" % (_oi_name, _oi_name)); continue
        _oi_end = src.find("\n", _oi_raise)
        _oi_guard = ('    # %s: once-only rule - if the %s buff is still active, reject WITHOUT consuming (no timer refresh).\n'
                     '    _bs_now = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n'
                     '    for _bs_b in player.get("active_buffs", []):\n'
                     '        if _bs_b.get("type") == "%s" and _bs_b.get("item_id") == "%s":\n'
                     '            _bs_exp = _bs_b.get("expires_at")\n'
                     '            if (not _bs_exp) or (str(_bs_exp) >= _bs_now):\n'
                     '                raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="%s is already active - wait for the effect to wear off.")\n' % (_oi_marker, _oi_name, _oi_type, _oi_id, _oi_name))
        src = src[:_oi_end + 1] + _oi_guard + src[_oi_end + 1:]
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ONCE_ONLY_%s_OK" % _oi_id.upper()); _once_done.append(_oi_id)
    if len(_once_done) == 4:
        landed.append("onceonly")
    elif _once_done:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ONCE_ONLY_PARTIAL: " + ",".join(_once_done))

    if src == orig:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_ALREADY_APPLIED")
        return 0
    try:
        compile(src, "server.py", "exec")
    except SyntaxError as e:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_SYNTAX_FAIL: %s (file NOT written)" % e)
        return 1
    SRV.write_text(src)
    if len(landed) == 7:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_OK")
    else:
        print("BROWN_SUGAR_ITEM_PARTIAL: " + ",".join(landed))
    return 0

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
